{"reference":"1 Chronicles 10","book":"1 Chronicles","chapter":10,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"historical_context","title":"Saul’s Death Interpreted","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The chapter’s final verses do more than recount Saul’s defeat and death: they interpret it. Saul’s death is attributed to unfaithfulness—specifically, not keeping the LORD’s word, seeking counsel from a medium, and failing to seek the LORD. The account therefore presents the transfer of the kingdom to David as part of this stated judgment on Saul.","verse_refs":["1 Chronicles 10:13-14"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_chronicles_010_314e8e3f23e8c87ea95ec56c"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}